That's already in the code! The deduplication is checking if the same key was seen in the last 5 minutes and dropping repeats:

```javascript
const last = seenKey.get(event.key);
if (last !== undefined && event.at - last < 5) {
  return [];
}
seenKey.set(event.key, event.at);
```

The verify.js tests confirm it's working correctly—it drops repeats within the 5-minute window but delivers again once that window passes.
